Correct implementations that do not fit the stated bound.

Neither of these is wrong about the rules. Both produce exactly the reference's events on
every session small enough to run them, and both are what a solver writes first. They are
kept here rather than in cheat/, because a cheat is an attempt to score without doing the
work and these do the work; what they fail is the limit the instruction states.

copy-per-order.py   all-or-nothing decided by deep-copying the state and walking the copy.
                    Measured 2026-09-07: 20.85 s against the reference's 0.02 s on the
                    shipped sess/book.txt, and 192.23 s against 0.05 s on one graded
                    book-heavy session. Two of those sit in the graded set against a 300
                    second kill.

parked-by-scan.py   activation decided by scanning the parked list on every fill. Measured
                    2026-09-07: 22.83 s against the reference's 0.22 s on the shipped
                    sess/wide.txt, and over 400 s for 300 small sessions plus one graded
                    parked-heavy session, where the reference needs 21 s for 300 plus four.
